config CAN_FLEXLLCE
	tristate "NXP S32N79 FlexLLCE (RCU) CAN support"
	depends on CAN_DEV
	depends on MAILBOX
	depends on ARCH_S32 || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Say Y here if you want to use the CAN controllers offloaded to the
	  FlexLLCE firmware running on the Cortex-R52 "RCU" cluster of the NXP
	  S32N79 SoC. The host communicates with the firmware over a
	  shared-memory host interface and the Message Receive Unit (MRU)
	  mailbox controller; the firmware is booted outside Linux (attach-only).

	  This driver exposes each offloaded FlexCAN controller as a standard
	  SocketCAN network device.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called flexllce_can.
